-# Task contract — player metric directions
+# Task contract — Ball actions, a new player metric
 
 objective: >
-  Appearances, minutes per appearance and the share of team goals carry the direction the
-  catalogue's own rule gives them (is more of it better, all else equal: yes), their
-  interpretations stop calling them neither good nor bad, and the `direction` description no
-  longer names a position-dependent share as neutral.
+  The catalogue gains two player metrics: ball_actions_player, the passes, shots, dribbles,
+  tackles, interceptions, blocks and saves a player made, and ball_actions_per90, the same per 90
+  minutes played. The generator writes both into the player season models; the count is served in
+  mart_player_profile and the per 90 in the position-peer comparison, as every existing count and
+  per-90 metric is. A hand-worked answer key proves both values.
 
 refs: >
-  #136, the Player page review, where the catalogue's player metrics were listed (directions,
-  interpretation texts and the description sentence approved in chat, 2026-11-01; this MR's plan
-  approved in chat, 2026-11-01). The approved player metric labels ship with the page that first
-  shows each metric and are recorded on #136.
+  #136, the Player page review, where the metric was defined (definition, texts, group and
+  direction approved in chat, 2026-11-01, recorded on #136; this MR's plan approved in chat,
+  2026-11-01).
 
